# Files Vercel must NOT skip.
#
# ★ THE BUG THIS EXISTS FOR.
#
# `static/` is the composed single-root deploy tree, and `.gitignore` excludes it
# because it is generated. But `vercel deploy` falls back to `.gitignore` when no
# `.vercelignore` is present, so the whole tree was filtered out of the UPLOAD.
#
# The failure was asymmetric, which is why it read as a font bug rather than a
# deploy bug: the HTML in `static/` was small enough to have been published
# already, but every file under `static/assets/` 404'd — including all 24 font
# files. The browser reported success on the page and 404 on the typeface, so
# English text fell back to a system font and looked like a missing `fontFamily`.
#
# `!` re-includes a path that an inherited rule would otherwise drop.
!static/
!static/**

# `dist/` is the raw Expo export that compose-static.sh merges into `static/`.
# It is kept for the same reason: the merge and the upload read it, and the
# deploy must not depend on a previously committed copy.
!dist/
!dist/**

# ★ THE FONTS LIVE UNDER A DIRECTORY LITERALLY NAMED `node_modules`.
#
# `.gitignore:20` is `node_modules/`, and an ignore pattern with no leading slash
# matches at ANY depth — so `static/assets/node_modules/**` was filtered out of
# the upload by the same rule that excludes the real dependency directory. The two
# `!static/**` negations above do not rescue it: a more specific ignore wins.
#
# The symptom was precisely the reported one: `/assets/assets/fonts/*.ttf`
# (Vazirmatn) resolved, because that path has no `node_modules` segment, while
# `/assets/node_modules/@expo-google-fonts/**` 404'd. Metro mirrors the package
# layout under `assets/`, so the Plus Jakarta Sans files an English screen needs
# were the only ones missing — and the page itself loaded fine.
#
# These re-include the ASSET copy only. The real dependency tree stays excluded —
# and it has to be excluded HERE, positively, not left to `.gitignore`:
#
# ★ AN `!` RULE CANNOT RE-OPEN A CHILD OF AN EXCLUDED PARENT.
#
# `.vercelignore` and `.gitignore` are merged, and gitignore semantics say a
# negated pattern has no effect if its parent directory is excluded. So the order
# that actually works is: exclude `node_modules` positively, then re-include the
# two asset mirrors. Without the explicit ignore below, the negations alone leave
# the uploader's decision to whichever file it read last.
node_modules
!static/assets/node_modules/
!static/assets/node_modules/**
!dist/assets/node_modules/
!dist/assets/node_modules/**
